I was wondering if anyone has any easy workarounds for querying the soilgrids.org <http://soilgrids.org> database for soil hydraulic properties when running the argument 'soilgrids =1' in any of the microclimate functions (e.g., micro_NCEP, micro_era5). At the moment, I query SoilGrids via the WCS service (maps.isric.org <http://maps.isric.org>) for bdod, clay, silt, and sand at standard depths, run NicheMapR::pedotransfer to derive PE/BB/BD/KS, then run the microclimate model with soilgrids = 0 and pass those soil parameters directly. This takes some time. Do you know of a better workaround or a more direct link? It's been about 3 weeks since the argument/link has been down.

Best,

Kris

